WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.550
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.550
But I have one too.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.350
Nice to meet you.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.460
What?  Then you're also...

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.200
But a bounty hunter's duty is 
to capture those who have Ignis.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.400
Fine.  I'll take you on.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.200
I admire you for defeating 
the ones who made us suffer.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.570
You gave me a path when 
I couldn't move forward.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.050
No matter how cornered he was...

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.800
...Go Onizuka was an independent duelist who 
believed in his own strength to the end!

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
Where's that person who gave me courage?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.610
Yes.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.030
The Lost Incident derailed Playmaker's life.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:58.500
For Playmaker, a duel 
means the same as living.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.890
Winning duels verifies his sense of self.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.140
And losing means losing yourself.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.790
His determination and persistence to win...

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:15.220
I believe this is the secret 
to Playmaker's power.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:21.080
I don't know what the Lost 
Incident victims had to endure.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:27.070
But I didn't start dueling halfheartedly.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:33.070
But I'm now here to be myself.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.370
To prove that I'm the strongest!

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.130
For the thirst for victory 
that's deep in my heart!

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:48.020
Go Onizuka is betting his life to dueling, 
so I won't take a single step back from you!

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.260
Battle!

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.790
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle attacks Heatleo!

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.960
Take this!  Jurassic Howl!

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.070
I end my turn.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.450
Go Onizuka...  I want to duel the real you.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.050
And I'll fight the real you and win!

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.700
Because I have a reason why I can't lose too!

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.120
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:47.330
Our lives aren't forever

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:54.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:01.420
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:07.990
Sharing hope for the future

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:14.730
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:21.970
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:28.680
I want to share your pain

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.460
We've rescued the children.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.450
They're all alive.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.660
What's your name?

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.160
Homura...  Takeru Homura...

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.630
Takeru, how old are you?

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.100
I'm six.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.470
Do you know your address?

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.420
Yes.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.980
Takeru!

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.810
Grandpa!  Grandma!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.250
Are you okay, Takeru?

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.270
I'm fine.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.590
Thank goodness.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.060
Truly.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.800
Where's Mom and Dad?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:04.320
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Link Fire's Return!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.020
I Special Summon a Salamangreat 
Link Monster from my graveyard!

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:16.180
I select Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:26.100
When this effect Special Summons a Link 
Monster, you take 200 damage per Link Marker!

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.510
Heatleo is Link 3!

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.240
So you take 600 damage!

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:41.920
When this effect Special Summons Heatleo, it 
can't attack or use its effects this turn.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.910
If we fail to capture the 
Ignis, Chief Zaizen will...

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.860
What's Playmaker's status?

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.100
He's moving through LINK VRAINS.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:55.100
He might get demoted again.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.280
I won't let that happen!  
I must protect the Chief!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:05.020
Even if you keep resurrecting 
it, I'll keep pummeling it.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.110
Go ahead and try!

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.550
It'll be good training, senpai!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.340
An attack from outside?

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:19.060
How could you resort to dirty tricks?

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.510
What?

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:23.990
Attacks from outside during 
a duel are inexcusable!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.030
I misjudged you!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:30.770
You must think lowly of me 
if you think I did that.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.680
I won't let Chief Zaizen be demoted!

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.600
Chief, don't worry.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.640
No one will take your seat again!

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.280
Stop the attack!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.770
Hayami!  What did you do?

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.500
N-Nothing...  Umm...

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:09.060
Or else, you'll be...

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.930
I'll be fine.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.740
How's Go Onizuka?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.480
Go Onizuka is fine!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.380
He's back in the duel!

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:24.380
When duelists are fighting 
seriously, don't interfere.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.380
I'm sorry.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.690
Come to the office when this is done.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.750
Okay.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.630
He voluntarily protected us.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:42.030
He didn't do those attacks.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:47.750
Yeah.  The Go Onizuka I 
know wouldn't do that.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.720
Here I go, Go Onizuka!

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.450
Yeah!  Bring it!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:57.170
I activate the Field Spell, 
Salamangreat Sanctuary!

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:03.340
When I Link Summon a 
Salamangreat Link Monster...

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:10.740
...I can use a Salamangreat Link Monster on 
my field with the same name to Link Summon!

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.450
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:20.750
I set Salamangreat Heatleo 
in the Link Marker!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.360
Reincarnation Link Summon!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.100
Be reborn!

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:30.430
Link 3 Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.600
Reincarnation Link Summon?

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:49.100
Reincarnation Link Summoned Heatleo's effect!

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:55.310
Your monster's ATK become the same 
as a monster in my graveyard!

00:08:55.820 --> 00:09:03.490
Your King T Wrextle's ATK become the same as 
my graveyard's Salamangreat Meer - which is 800!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.460
T Wrextle only has 800 ATK?

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.650
See that?  This is-

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.330
This is Soulburner's special technique!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.080
C'mon, don't hog the spotlight!

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:20.570
I thought it'd be awkward and pretentious 
if you brag about your own technique.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.670
I was being nice.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.580
Since King T Wrextle is down to 800 ATK...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:30.050
...you'll use Heatleo to 
destroy it and damage my LP.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.590
But I won't let you!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.880
Here I go!  Battle-

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.190
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle's 
effect activates!

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:42.390
During this battle, Jack 
Jaguar must attack first!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.900
What?  Jack Jaguar has to attack first?

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.420
Jack Jaguar has 1800 ATK.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:55.140
And due to World Dino Wrestling's 
effect, only one monster can attack.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:00.110
If you don't attack, Jack Jaguar 
is destroyed at the end of battle.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.080
Of course I'll attack!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:08.250
Salamangreat Jack Jaguar attacks 
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:14.120
When my Dinowrestler battles a 
monster with equal or higher ATK...

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:20.970
...I can send Dinowrestler Martial Ankylo in 
my hand to the graveyard to activate its effect!

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:25.890
King T Wrextle can't be 
destroyed in this battle!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.740
But you still take damage!

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:39.620
Due to Martial Ankylo's effect, 
your monster's ATK are halved!

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:44.730
Heatleo's effect ends!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.830
King T Wrextle's ATK returns to normal!

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.640
His Dinowrestler Deck is pretty tough.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:58.310
This isn't the time to be in awe.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:04.040
But it's true that Go Onizuka 
has mastered his new deck.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:07.280
Go Onizuka truly is impressive.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.750
I won't be defeated that easily.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.980
I end my turn!

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:15.720
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:22.670
He has Heatleo with 2300 ATK 
and Jack Jaguar with 900.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:27.870
And I have King T Wrextle with 3000 ATK.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:35.290
In my previous life as an entertainer, I 
would use King T Wrextle to attack Heatleo.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.610
To create a highlight when 
our ace monsters clash.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:47.150
But now that I'm a bounty hunter, I'll aim 
for a guaranteed win instead of a highlight!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:48.620
Battle!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:54.960
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle 
attacks Salamangreat Jack Jaguar!

00:11:54.960 --> 00:12:02.330
Due to the Field Spell World Dino 
Wrestling's effect, it gains 200 ATK!

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:06.220
If this works, he'll take 2300 damage!

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.070
That's more than Soulburner's LP!

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:12.980
The Field Spell, Salamangreat 
Sanctuary's effect!

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:17.870
When I take battle damage, I pay 1000 LP!

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:26.460
My Salamangreat's ATK becomes 0, and 
I gain LP equal to the decrease!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.900
I wanted to finish him this turn, but...

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.620
The Field Spell's effect ends.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:42.870
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle's 
ATK return to normal.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:47.120
When a Dinowrestler Link Monster 
deals you battle damage...

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.710
...I Special Summon Dinowrestler Rambrachio 
from my hand in defense position!

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:03.260
Due to Rambrachio, effects can't affect 
all other Dinowrestlers next turn.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:10.540
So even if he uses Heatleo's effect 
again, T Wrextle is protected!

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.770
All right!  I end my turn!

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:19.010
Go Onizuka, I know how 
devoted you are to dueling.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.450
However...

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:31.390
I also have a reason why 
I can't afford to lose!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.080
Takeru!

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:49.450
Takeru, what are you doing here?

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.110
Come to school already.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:57.170
Kiku, I...  I'll go.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.080
I'm going.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:03.770
Really?  You finally feel like it?

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:07.210
But it's only four days 'til summer vacation.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.440
I don't care about summer vacation.

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.770
I'm leaving this city.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.340
What do you mean?

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.560
I'm not myself right now.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.220
This isn't the real me.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.800
What are you talking about?  
Takeru, you're you!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.450
That's why I'm leaving.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.920
Kiku, look after my Grandpa and Grandma.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.370
Takeru...

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.400
I don't know what's going on.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:50.470
But if that's your decision, good luck!

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:55.420
Because you look like you're full of life!

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.040
Thank you, Kiku.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.280
After the Lost Incident, I hated everything.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.750
Anything I did was halfhearted.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:16.050
I stopped dueling and sealed 
away my past memories.

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:22.590
But during that time, I learned that duelists 
were fighting against those who made me suffer.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.650
I couldn't sit still, so I came to Den City.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:31.370
Soulburner, I know how you feel, but-

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.600
I can't forget about the past!

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.070
Starting today, this is your home.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:39.090
Why?

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.930
You're living with us.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:46.810
My time has remained stopped since that day.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:59.040
Your Mom and Dad searched for you every day.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.310
And...

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:04.970
And they were in an accident.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:12.940
After losing my parents, all I 
had left were my grandparents...

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:16.650
...and dueling, which I 
vowed never to do again!

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:25.060
To make time move again, 
all I can do is duel!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.360
I activate my Skill!

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:36.330
By dropping my LP to 100, I draw one 
card for every 1000 LP that I paid!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:39.330
Burn your soul, Soulburner!

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.570
Show a miracle!  Burning Draw!

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:50.440
I activate Rise of the 
Salamangreat from my hand!

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:58.480
I tribute monsters from my hand and 
field whose total Level equals at least

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.930
the monster I'm Ritual Summoning!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:06.670
I Ritual Summon a Salamangreat 
Ritual Monster from my hand!

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:11.470
But when there's a Salamangreat 
Link Monster on our field...

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:17.210
I can return Salamangreat monsters in my 
graveyard to my deck instead of tributing!

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:24.450
I return Level 4 Salamangreat Falco and 
Jack Jaguar in my graveyard to my deck!

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:27.390
Ritual Summon!

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.390
Rise, Level 8!

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.160
Jade wings clad in flames!

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:36.590
Salamangreat Emerald Eagle!

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.160
But my T Wrextle has 3000 ATK!

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.270
That's more than Emerald Eagle!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:51.780
Exactly.  But that doesn't matter!

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.030
What?

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:57.080
Salamangreat Emerald 
Eagle's effect activates!

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.990
I tribute a Salamangreat 
Link Monster on my field!

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:06.190
You tributed your own ace monster?

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.160
Go, Soulburner!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.430
Battle!

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:15.830
Salamangreat Emerald Eagle attacks 
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:20.770
Due to Emerald Eagle's effect, 
King T Wrextle is destroyed...

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:23.970
...and you take damage equal to its ATK!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:24.980
What?

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.180
Emerald Overload!

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.820
Well done!

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.740
I lost...

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:02.540
Go Onizuka!

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:10.160
For me, you're the hero who defeated 
the Hanoi and saved LINK VRAINS.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:12.280
That hasn't changed.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:19.210
But to get my real self back, 
I have to keep winning!

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.500
And that's the same for you-

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.970
What are you trying to say?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.180
Listen, I'll tell you this.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:29.540
No one can always win.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.510
Everyone experiences defeat.

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:36.200
Will defeat rot you?  Or will 
you use it as a springboard?

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.320
When you lose, the true you is revealed!

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:48.520
He must lose a lot to be such a sore loser.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.480
You're pretty condescending.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.000
Not really.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:03.260
It's rough going.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:05.600
That's the lower area.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.820
Which Kusanagi talked about.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.200
Yeah.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:19.390
The sphere in the restricted area's bottom 
level should have a gate at its center.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:27.130
I'm spooked!

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:29.730
Yeah.  I sense something bad.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:30.970
Really bad!

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.420
Let's withdraw.  Right?

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:00.960
I've caught the bounty.

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:26.180
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:32.890
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:36.390
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:39.530
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:44.130
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:47.100
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:57.980
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:01.120
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:05.080
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:11.030
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:14.300
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:42.100
Those he targets lose by the count of three.

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:44.740
He sold his soul for money.

00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:50.320
Known as a crafty Player Killer, 
no one knows his identity.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:54.510
Those he meets die in the end.

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:58.050
He'll do anything to fulfill his mission.

00:23:58.050 --> 00:24:02.540
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Bounty Hunter Blood Shepherd

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:04.490
Into the VRAINS!
